# Anchored to the repository root. A bare `data/` matches a directory named
# `data` at ANY depth, which silently ignored `infrastructure/data/` -- the
# committed dataset-licence declaration and its JSON schema. Those are
# governance artifacts CI must see, not datasets, and because an ignored path
# is refused by `git add` without `-f`, task 7.1 could tick complete while its
# deliverable never reached CI. Real data stays ignored: the root `data/` tree
# by this rule, and every dataset artifact by the extension patterns above
# (e.g. `data_fabric/feast/data/demand_signals.parquet` via `*.parquet`).
/data/
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Secrets (NEVER commit)
.env
.env.cloud
.env.gcp
.env.gcp.local
# ADR-039: workflow-written, transient per deploy — never commit
.env.gcp.version
.env.local
*.key
*.pem
vault-token

